# CVEs accepted in the upstream quay.io/keycloak/keycloak image (libraries bundled by Keycloak itself, not by
# this project). Remove each entry once a Keycloak release ships the fixed library.
# Reviewed 2026-11-18 against Keycloak 26.8.2 (weekly scan of gointerop/gointerop-keycloak, run 43946390208).
#
# Upgrading from 26.7.4 to 26.8.2 fixed every entry accepted on 2026-09-24 (netty-handler CVE-2026-75595,
# bcprov CVE-2026-8763 / CVE-2026-13506, mssql-jdbc CVE-2025-59250, pcre2 CVE-2026-86145 / CVE-2026-89161),
# so they were removed. Unfixed OS findings (sqlite-libs, java-21-openjdk-headless CVE-2026-91403) need no entry:
# the CI gate runs with ignore-unfixed.

# guava 33.6.0-jre (/opt/keycloak/lib/lib/main, fixed in 33.7.2): denial of service via unthrottled allocation
# while deserializing CompactHashMap / CompactHashSet / MapMakerInternalMap from a Java serialization stream.
# Only reachable when untrusted Java-serialized data is deserialized; Keycloak does not accept Java serialization
# from clients, and its Infinispan caches use ProtoStream. Replacing the jar inside the Quarkus build is not
# worth the risk for a DoS. Expires so the next monthly CVE iteration re-checks the Keycloak release.
CVE-2026-102554 exp:2027-01-05
